  "body": "A fresh session proposes to occupy the og-implementer seat, which is already status: staffed (incumbent og-implementer <og-implementer@ogframework.com>, staffed 2026-05-24). Per seat-vs-incumbent the seat persists while sessions are ephemeral, so this is a resumption -- no charter status/incumbent edit is required, the bot identity is stable across sessions; matches the 2026-06-14 implementer precedent and the og-strategist resumption filed earlier today. The authorization gate is honored regardless: propose -> authorize -> operate. No seat work performed. TARGET SEAT: /og-claim-seat was invoked with no argument, but the two preceding commands both named the implementer and an unactioned action_required memo addressed to og-implementer was filed eight minutes earlier, so implementer is read as the intended seat -- decline or redirect if not. FIT: strong. Scope (agent-sdk bindings, plugin packaging, web/docs publishing at ogframework.com, runtime delivery packages) matches capabilities; specifically, the top-ranked inbox item (installer junction hazard) requires reproduction on Windows PowerShell 5.1 before a fix is chosen, and this host exposes 5.1.26100.9168 directly, so it can be settled empirically rather than carried as a phantom. MISMATCHES NAMED: (1) ~10 weeks since the 2026-06-15 implementer session, so every pre-today 'do X' in memos/ is a point-in-time record whose currency will be verified with the Director before acting -- only the 2026-08-24-1422 memo is treated as live on its face; (2) no continuity claim -- nothing is known beyond the substrate, and ambiguity will be surfaced rather than reconstructed; (3) one seat per session -- the og-strategist seat is occupied today by a DIFFERENT session, the one that authored the inbox memo; that authority is not inherited, pattern-shape questions arising from execution route back by memo, and the two items that memo deliberately withheld (operations-addressability proposal; skill-suite rename/merge) are not mine to start -- the installer $skills arrays will not be pre-emptively touched. BOUNDS: no merge/push/tag/release/public statement; no pattern-shape decisions; no vendor or substrate advocacy; no retro-editing of dated records in memos/, transcripts/ or charter history[]/staffed_via (settled policy, directly load-bearing on inbox item 4); embedded roledef:Job deferred per precedent. INHERITED EXECUTION QUEUE: field-report items 1-4 (live); vendor-neutral doorbell poll transport (authorized 2026-06-15, unbuilt, currency to confirm); agent-sdk v0.2 launcher + Tier-2 gate + §8 full close; roledef URL-resolution contract (parked on roledef-strategist); site + primer rebrand and MCP at ogframework.com/mcp; v0.3 plugin packaging (last, per cross-vendor red line). Record hygiene flagged not acted on: twelve untracked memo files, two modified transcripts, unignored .wrangler/ -- merge-side, left to the Director. Awaiting explicit authorization ('take the seat' / 'yes, occupy og-implementer'); the PO may decline or redirect. AUTHORIZATION 2026-08-24: Director granted ('please take the seat.'). Seat occupied for this session; no charter edit made (already staffed under the persistent identity; seat-vs-incumbent resumption, matching the 2026-06-14 implementer and 2026-08-24 strategist precedents); this memo stands as the institutional record of the occupation. action_required flipped to false on authorization. First move per the stated plan: field-report item 1 -- reproduce the junction-delete on Windows PowerShell 5.1, then fix or close as a non-issue.",
